<!--
  PATHS ARE RELATIVE, DELIBERATELY (fixed 2026-09-10).

  This file used to use absolute /media/fat/... paths, described as "belt-and-
  braces -- honored verbatim on every Main version". That reasoning only holds if
  the games live on the SD card. MEASURED: with games on a USB drive, /media/fat
  paths do not exist, NONE of the file entries load, and the core falls back to
  autoloading a boot.rom -- finding the CONSUMER SONY BIOS in games/PSX, because
  the core reports its CONF_STR name to Main as "PSX". Symptom: the PlayStation
  logo and startup sound instead of the Konami BIOS.

  Relative paths resolve against whichever storage the launcher was started from,
  so this works on SD and USB alike. For an SD-only setup the equivalent absolute
  path is /media/fat/<path below>.

  Belt-and-braces that does work: put a copy of the standard BIOS at
  games/System573/boot.rom. If Main resolves this core's HomeDir from <setname>,
  that autoload finds the Konami BIOS rather than the Sony one.
-->
<!--
  TEST B: launch hyperbbc as a STANDALONE CONSOLE core via .mgl (is_arcade_type=0).
  Loads the SAME known-good data the arcade .mra uses (stock BIOS + the real hyperbbc
  flash + nvram), NO CD. Purpose: prove the .mgl/console launch mechanism + the new F0
  BIOS CONF_STR entry actually load the BIOS (the prior bare .mgl black-screened because
  there was no F0 -> BIOS never loaded). Expected: boots+runs hyperbbc exactly like the
  .mra. If this works, the mechanism is sound and Test C (hypbbc2p install) can proceed.

  Requires: _Console/Konami_System_573.rbf (deploy the build there) + the listed files
  staged under /media/fat/games/System573/.
-->
<mistergamedescription>
  <rbf>_Console/Konami_System_573</rbf>
  <!-- setname: own HomeDir + own config namespace. Without it the core's CONF_STR name
       ("PSX") makes Main (a) resolve relative paths against games/PSX (silent ENOENT on
       some Main versions -> ZERO files load -> the 2026-06-07 black+audio loop, which was
       the consumer Sony boot.rom autoload dying on 573 fabric), and (b) blind-load the
       consumer PSX core's saved status bits from config/PSX.CFG (Boot Device/PAL/Turbo
       pollution). Paths are ABSOLUTE as belt-and-braces -- honored verbatim on every
       Main version (fleet precedent: the dvd core hit the same class). -->
  <setname>System573</setname>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="0" path="games/System573/573bios.bin"/>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="2" path="games/System573/hbbflash.bin"/>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="3" path="games/System573/hbbnvram.bin"/>
  <reset delay="1"/>
</mistergamedescription>
